Krohnkite Effect rewrite

Derived from Krohnkite by Eon S. Jeon and Vjatcheslav V. Kolchkov.
The original MIT copyright and permission notice is retained in LICENSE.
The upstream source is pinned at .repo/krohnkite, as recorded in upstreams.json.

KWin runtime resources and settings retain upstream code and attribution:
res/popup.qml, dbus.qml, dragpreview.qml, config.ui, and config.xml are copied
without modification into packages/kwin/assets. res/shortcuts.qml retains all
39 handlers, action names, labels, and SPDX notices; only its 25 nonempty default
bindings are adjusted to Meta plus one key, with the other 14 left unbound.
The main QML entry and package metadata are adapted for the Effect runtime.
Original SPDX notices
remain in copied QML files, including the 2026 Krohnkite contributors notice in
dragpreview.qml.

docs/images/screenshot.png and docs/images/conf.png are unchanged copies of
the upstream img/ files referenced by its README. They are historical upstream
documentation examples. The repository's original MIT notice is retained in
LICENSE; no separate image license is declared upstream. RESOURCE-MIGRATION.md
records the source revision, resource mappings, hashes, and distribution use.

This distribution bundles Effect 4.0.0 by Effectful Technologies Inc.
Effect is licensed under MIT. Its license is included in release packages.
The current v4 source is pinned at .repo/effect. The archived effect-smol
repository is not the canonical v4 source.

The Qt bundle includes generator state-machine helpers from @babel/helpers
8.0.5. These helpers are licensed under MIT, copyright 2014-present Sebastian
McKenzie and other contributors; the regenerator helpers are also copyright
2014-present Facebook, Inc. The complete notice is included at
licenses/Babel-helpers-LICENSE.txt in the installed KWin package.
